      players: 'Minimum Players: 2\nMaximum Players: 6\nOptimal Players: 4 (partnerships)\nPartnerships: With 4 or 6 players, partners sit opposite.',
      deck: 'Type: Three standard 52-card decks plus 6 jokers (162 cards total). Twos and jokers are wild.',
      equipment: 'Three 52-card decks, 6 jokers, score sheet, table space.',
      dealing: 'Cards per Player: 15 each for 2–5 players; 13 each for 6 players. One card turned face up to start discard pile; remainder forms stock. Dealing clockwise.',
    },
    turnFlow: '1. Deal: 15 cards each (2–5 players) or 13 each (6 players). One card up for discard pile; rest is stock.\n2. Turn: Draw two from stock (or take discard pile under rules, or take one card to add to existing sequence), meld if desired, discard one.\n3. Melds: Groups (3+ same rank, max 2 wilds) and sequences (3–7 same suit, no wilds). Seven-card group = canasta; seven-card sequence = samba.\n4. Going out: Must have two sambas, or two canastas, or one of each; then meld all or all but one and discard the last.\n5. Scoring: Card values plus bonuses (samba 1500, pure canasta 500, mixed 300, going out 200); first to 10,000 wins.',
